---
description: Keep the code clean and refactor proactively, in bounded steps
alwaysApply: true
---

Always keep the code clean. Refactor proactively, but only within reach
of the change you are making. KISS and YAGNI from `general.mdc` still
apply.

- Leave every file you touch cleaner than you found it.
- In or near the code you change, refactor when you see:
  - the same logic a third time (rule of three): extract it once;
  - dead code, unused exports, files or deps: delete them;
  - unclear names: rename them;
  - long functions doing several things: split them;
  - leaky boundaries, such as a package importing past the direction in
    DES-015: move the code to the package that owns it.
- Refactors preserve behavior. Tests are green before and after; add a
  test first when the code you refactor has none.
- Commit refactors separately from features or fixes (`refactor: ...`),
  so each diff does one thing.
- No speculative abstractions, layers or options "for later".
- Do not refactor code far from the task just because you saw it. Record a
  bigger refactor you skip as a backlog item or a DES-007 ledger entry with
  a revisit trigger, and mention it in your report.
